      "problem": "Factor $\\frac{{u}^{3}}{8}-1.$",
      "worked_solution": "The difference of cubes formula is given by\n\n$$\n{a}^{3}-{b}^{3}=(a-b)({a}^{2}+ab+{b}^{2}).\n$$\n\nNotice that we can write our expression as a difference of cubes, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{u}^{3}}{8}-1={(\\frac{u}{2})}^{3}-{1}^{3}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor our expression using the difference of cubes formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{u}^{3}}{8}-1 & ={(\\frac{u}{2})}^{3}-{1}^{3} \\\\  & =(\\frac{u}{2}-1)({(\\frac{u}{2})}^{2}+\\frac{u}{2}\\cdot 1+{(1)}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{u}{2}-1)(\\frac{{u}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{u}{2}+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
